Z||000000||Loki||06-17-2001||08:21 PM||||Whats the fix for the wobbly steering colum?<P><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tweek||06-17-2001||08:35 PM||||I havn't done it, but from what I can tell...<P>If your experience is low, then the easiest thing is to swap it out with another one. If you want to go through the painstaking task of fixing it, there are 4 torx head bolts buried inside the column that have come loose, Orge's cave has *Excellent* notes on how to fix it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroHarry||06-17-2001||08:59 PM||||Loki,<BR>There is a special tool sold by Snap - On that will remove the pivot pins in your colunm to allow access to those four Torx bolts. (without it you'll never get to them at all).<BR>If you need to borrow mine drop me an e-mail but there only about $28.00  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> we can work it out thru the mail.....<P>------------------<BR><B>Harry Waggoner</B><BR>1985 GT 264K+ <I>FOCOSEVA,FOCOA</I><BR><B>"Im not driving to fast, Im flying to low!"</B>||||reg||1
